From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 05:59:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: cubie-a7s: Enable the PRCM I2C
 buses

On the Cubie A7S the AXP318W PMIC is wired to S_TWI0 on PL0/PL1 and
the HUSB311 Type-C port controller to S_TWI1 on PL12/PL13.

Enable both buses with these pins, so that the PMIC and the port
controller can be described on them.

The PMIC and the port controller nodes come with the PMIC and the USB
support.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; PL0/PL1 and PL12/PL13
are muxed to r_i2c0 and r_i2c1, and the Type-C controller answers at
0x4e on the second bus.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts     | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
index d812f45e1751..ad82a4425039 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
@@ -98,6 +98,18 @@ &osc {
 	clock-frequency = <26000000>;
 };
 
+&r_i2c0 {
+	pinctrl-names = "default";
+	pinctrl-0 = <&r_i2c0_pl_pins>;
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&r_i2c1 {
+	pinctrl-names = "default";
+	pinctrl-0 = <&r_i2c1_pl12_pins>;
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &rtc {
 	clocks = <&r_ccu CLK_BUS_R_RTC>, <&osc>,
 		 <&r_ccu CLK_R_AHB>, <&ext_osc32k>;
